db/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362013 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362013 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362013 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362013 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186361039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362013 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "259f1c7d-faf1-5444-bcc6-52bd54d6cb93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362293 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186361995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362293 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98344" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362293 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362293 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & f(-3,-1,-2)=1, &  & {f}_{x}(-3,-1,-2)=4, \\\\  & {f}_{y}(-3,-1,-2)=-3, &  & {f}_{z}(-3,-1,-2)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-3,-1,-2)$ estimate the value of $f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362293 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "52cca677-fb8e-5fcb-a6f2-9f28e4bd054c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362293 #edb/ref 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-3,-1,-2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(-3,-1,-2)+∇f(-3,-1,-2)\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩ \\\\  & =f(-3,-1,-2) \\\\  & \\,+⟨{f}_{x}(-3,-1,-2),{f}_{y}(-3,-1,-2),{f}_{z}(-3,-1,-2)⟩\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+3,y+1,z+2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=-3.04,$ $y=-1.02,$ and $z=-2.03$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3.04,-1.02,-2.03) & ≈1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3.04+3,-1.02+1,-2.03+2⟩ \\\\  & =1+⟨4,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.04,-0.02,-0.03⟩ \\\\  & =1-0.16+0.06+0.06 \\\\  & =0.96\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
